    "result_text": "The change is complete and all tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule that rejects creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the existing conventions for the other business-rule rejections (`DuplicateHouseholdException`, `DuplicateTelephoneException`).\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`rest/advice/CityAtCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring `DuplicateHouseholdException`, thrown when a create targets a city at capacity.\n\n2. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityAtCapacityException` that returns 409 with an `errors` array naming the `city` field, consistent with the other 409 handlers.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `CITY_CAPACITY = 50` constant and a `rejectCityAtCapacity(city)` method that counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed comparison via the existing `normalizeName`, matching how `nextCustomerCode` counts a city) and throws when the count is \u2265 50. The check is invoked in `addOwner` after the required-field/household validation and before telephone processing.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` test (fill a city to 50, then expect the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
